            <div xml:id="d852">

                <pb facs="0998" n="880" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg880"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00 R 296/2600: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Armour</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase—Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-01-08T16:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 8,
                                1929—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 8—1:25
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>10. Reparation 164.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Is the understanding correct that the six Governments, before proceeding to
                    appoint Americans whom they select, will submit their names to the
                    Department?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Armour</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
